Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 EU language select (CNTY_SEL) fills 16:9

The EU language select (CNTY_SEL, mode file 0x165) ran with gutter 0, a 4:3
picture pillarboxed on a 16:9 screen. It now takes the menu gutter
(port/options/widescreen.c) and fills it:

- The scrolling background repeats every 96 pixels (a pattern of hexagons, as
  the player name screen's, patch 0087): DW3_WIDE_PERIODIC adds, at draw
  time, the copies of its parts moved by whole periods that show in a gutter.
- The three panels (the header band, the logo band, the flags' panel) are
  straight lines that run to the 4:3 edges: DW3_WIDE_WINGS repeats their outer
  8 columns across the gutters, so each runs to the picture's edge (the flags'
  panel also covers the logo band's overhang that sat past the 4:3 edge).
- The fade-out polygon reaches the picture's edges.

The panels' contents, the options and the cursor keep their places (the 4:3
middle). Off, nothing changes. The US disc has no language select; the mode is
never entered there.

--- a/include/menus/country_select.h
+++ b/include/menus/country_select.h
@@ -14,6 +14,15 @@
 
 #include "engine/game.h"
 
+#if PORT_HOST
+#include "port_widescreen.h"
+#else
+#define DW3_WIDE_PERIODIC(sheet, frame, x, y, dx, dy) (sheet)
+#define DW3_WIDE_WINGS(sheet, frame, x) (sheet)
+#endif
+/* The background repeats every 96 pixels, both ways (CNTY_SEL_drawBackground) */
+#define CNTY_SEL_BACKGROUND_PERIOD 96
+
 /*
  * The screen's tasks use the engine states (task.h); the owner sets TASK_DONE
  * to make a task fade out, flash, or open/close its panel.
